kmscon-hangul (10.0.1-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Update libtsm subproject to v4.8.0 (statically linked). Includes
    libtsm 2753e37, which clears the character of the trailing cells of a
    wide glyph on write; fixes stale characters showing through Hangul
    text redrawn in place (e.g. nvim page up/down, tmux).

 -- JohnnyB <johnhsb@outlook.kr>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0900

kmscon-hangul (10.0.1-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * render/bbulk: clear stale double_width flag on overflow cells
    (cherry-picked from upstream ed7ba4c). Fixes half-glyph artifacts of
    wide (Hangul) characters left behind in blank cells after scrolling.

 -- JohnnyB <johnhsb@outlook.kr>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0900

kmscon-hangul (10.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream base: kmscon v10.0.1 (was v10.0.0)
  * Merge upstream session-management simplification: kmscon_session event
    callback removed; terminal now driven by direct terminal_activate() /
    terminal_deactivate() / terminal_add_display() / terminal_rm_display()
    calls from seat.c. IM composition flush-on-deactivate moved into
    terminal_deactivate() accordingly.
  * Merge upstream text-renderer simplification (tsm_screen_draw2 /
    kmscon_text_draw(txt, con)); rewrite IM preedit overlay to patch a copy
    of the whole-screen cell array instead of injecting via the old
    per-cell draw callback.
  * Merge upstream terminal blink support, ctrl+wheel zoom, and asciicast
    playback (unrelated to Hangul IM, carried through unchanged)
  * video/drm: drop our perform_modeset() use-after-free fix in favor of
    upstream's equivalent fix (refs_taken guard), which was added
    independently upstream for the same bug
  * Update libtsm subproject to v4.6.0 (statically linked)

 -- JohnnyB <johnhsb@outlook.kr>  Sat, 18 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0900

